## Phase 1 — Data Model & DB Setup (no user-facing change yet)

**Goal:** Add the new `Drop` collection/schema without touching any existing working feature.

Tasks:
1. Define a `Drop` document shape:
   - `youtubeVideoId` (string, unique)
   - `youtubeUrl` (string)
   - `publishedAt` (date — from YouTube)
   - `addedAt` (date — when our system created the Drop)
   - `expiresAt` (date — `addedAt + 5 days`)
   - `products`: array of `{ imageUrl, title, price, details, sizeOptions?, inStock }`
   - `status`: `"active" | "deleted_manually" | "expired"`
2. Create a **MongoDB TTL index** on `expiresAt` (expireAfterSeconds: 0) so Mongo auto-deletes the document itself once the time passes — no cron job needed for deletion.
3. Write this as a migration/setup script the agent can run once, not inline app logic.
4. **Do not** build ingestion, admin UI, or storefront UI yet.

**Stop condition:** Confirm the collection + TTL index exist in MongoDB Atlas (check the index in Atlas UI or via a script) before moving to Phase 2.

