## Phase 3 — Rewrite Core Backend Endpoints (FastAPI → Next.js API routes)

**Goal:** Move existing product/catalog CRUD endpoints from Python/FastAPI to Node/Next.js API routes, one resource at a time, so the site keeps working throughout.

Tasks (do sub-steps one at a time, testing each before the next):
1. List every existing FastAPI endpoint currently in use (agent should scan the Python codebase first and produce this list before writing any new code).
2. For each endpoint group (e.g. products, categories, orders/inquiries, admin auth):
   - Recreate it as a Next.js API route with the same request/response shape, so the frontend doesn't need changes yet.
   - Point it at the same MongoDB database (no data migration needed, same DB).
   - Test that endpoint in isolation (Postman/curl) before moving to the next group.
3. Only after **all** groups are recreated and tested, switch the frontend's API base URL from the old Render URL to the new Vercel URL.
4. Keep the Render service running (but idle) until the new endpoints are confirmed fully working in production — do not delete/cancel Render yet.

**Stop condition:** Every old endpoint has a working Vercel equivalent, frontend is pointed at Vercel, and the site works end-to-end with zero calls going to Render.

